{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0CN6", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-universal-homeomorphisms-affine}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:78b96f45fb8552e4547cb22f275fac7f2dcb385d2484478894c2f6fd490b0995", "source_text": "Universal homeomorphisms of affine schemes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f5b0a4b362cc7112eeac397908d67f60a53ae354b771564903805c930bc085df", "unit_id": "tag:0CN6:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CN6", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ce7889f7407ea673731f21e523b1fcb5c599a22c597e44befd7fc1e43c69d053", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we characterize universal homeomorphisms of affine schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5b94b2d106bf5c734874714bdef91efaa0a2f176b2401847926293208661be03", "unit_id": "tag:0CN6:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CN6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$f : \\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$B' \\subset B$", "MATH_0005": "$f' : \\Spec(B') \\to \\Spec(A)$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-subalgebra-inherits}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:91096de9f63e9ab148fa66091286267d2640f30af37d7fb40e2adc40d526909f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:84cc8ef1730db072af88f8d26d62e556da32ab7d6e17b12f2ae49280118dad70", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring map such that the induced morphism of\nschemes <MATH_0002> is a universal homeomorphism,\nresp.<SPACE_0001>a universal homeomorphism inducing isomorphisms on residue fields,\nresp.<SPACE_0002>universally closed,\nresp.<SPACE_0003>universally closed and universally injective.\nThen for any <MATH_0003>-subalgebra <MATH_0004>\nthe same thing is true for <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6641d408df333fdb0bc4585cfe48bf46c4edf64a572345fc70a7fcac069915f1", "unit_id": "tag:0CN7:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CN6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$B'$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$f'$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$B$", "MATH_0009": "$B'$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(B')$", "MATH_0011": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0012": "$A \\to B'$", "MATH_0013": "$f$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$f$", "MATH_0016": "$f'$", "MATH_0017": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0018": "$A \\to B'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-integral-universally-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-integral-permanence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-integral-overring-surjective}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-universally-injective}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-universal-homeomorphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0005": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0006": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:412b92e9cf144da1414a6d3281dc92327f5df472e21eca6af60128bcfae438d6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7450d46dde0e7adcdb9c63174c07dcc07b15de4790ced669b329bb64ef79d0e2", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is universally closed, then\n<MATH_0002> is integral over <MATH_0003> by Lemma <REF_0001>.\nHence <MATH_0004> is integral over <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006>\nis universally closed (by the same lemma).\nThis proves the case where <MATH_0007> is universally closed.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nContinuing, we see that <MATH_0008> is integral over <MATH_0009> \n(Algebra, Lemma <REF_0002>)\nwhich implies <MATH_0010> is surjective\n(Algebra, Lemma <REF_0003>).\nThus if <MATH_0011> induces purely inseparable extensions of residue fields,\nthen the same is true for <MATH_0012>. This proves the case\nwhere <MATH_0013> is universally closed and universally injective, see\nLemma <REF_0004>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nThe case where <MATH_0014> is a universal homeomorphism follows from\nthe remarks above, Lemma <REF_0005>,\nand the obvious observation that if <MATH_0015> is surjective, then so is <MATH_0016>.\n\n<STRUCT_0005><STRUCT_0006>\nIf <MATH_0017> induces isomorphisms on residue fields, then\nso does <MATH_0018> (see argument in second paragraph).\nIn this way we see that the lemma holds in the remaining case.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:473c169c8b4535fb496da5939b1f87bcb40e6661dbbc492c703965ef574fea45", "unit_id": "tag:0CN7:proof"}
